vent. Since it's a clear decision stated as fact (\"从今天起\"), I'll note it as the speech event with the content.\n\nLet me also note:\n- 乔米 and 褚衡 had a shared drawer (一直共用的抽屉) - this is background revealed\n- 乔米 and 褚衡 had a shared red pen (共用的红笔) - background revealed\n- 乔米 was previously 褚衡's assistant (implied by her statement, and by him having a work badge with him)\n\nLet me think about the previous assistant relationship: \"不再给你做助理\" implies she WAS his assistant. This is established by her statement. But since this is implied rather than explicitly stated as past fact, I should be careful. The text says \"from today onwards, I no longer will be your assistant\" - this implies she was his assistant before. I can record this as background implied by the text.\n\nActually, let me be careful. The text says she is declaring she won't be his assistant \"从今天起\" (from today). The implication is that she was his assistant before. This is a reasonable inference from the text. I'll record it.\n\nLet me also note: 褚衡's behavior (not returning the badge, locking the drawer) is silent/non-verbal. His inner state is not stated, only his actions.\n\nLet me structure the facts:\n\n1. 乔米从工位夹上摘下工牌 - 已发生\n2. 乔米把工牌塞进褚衡摊开的掌心 - 已发生\n3. 乔米对褚衡说\"从今天起，我不再给你做助理\" - 已发生 (speech)\n4. 褚衡没有把工牌还回去 - 已发生\n5. 褚衡把工牌卡片翻过去 - 已发生\n6. 褚衡伸手把两人中间那条一直共用的抽屉锁上 - 已发生\n7. 两人中间有一条一直共用的抽屉 - (this is a state/relationship fact)\n8. 乔米站在原处看了褚衡两秒 - 已发生\n9. 乔米把桌上那支共用的红笔推进抽屉缝 - 已发生\n10. 乔米转身离开 - 已发生\n11. 两人共用的红笔 - relationship fact\n12. 乔米之前是褚衡的助理 - implied from the statement (speaker: 乔米)\n\nLet me finalize. I should be efficient and not over-split, but also not combine independent facts.\n\nLet me re-read and finalize:\n\nFact 1: 乔米从工位夹上摘下工牌，放进褚衡摊开的掌心。- Action combining two related physical acts.\nActually, the rules say \"每条事实只保留一个核心断言。同一句包含多个独立行动、状态或认知变化时必须拆开\". So:\n- 乔米把工牌从工位夹上摘下来\n- 乔米把工牌塞进褚衡摊开的掌心\nThese are sequential related actions but could be considered one continuous action. I'll combine them as one fact about 乔米 handing over the badge.\n\nActually, I'll split them into:\n- 乔米从工位夹上摘下工牌\n- 乔米将工牌塞进褚衡摊开的掌心\n\nFact 2: 乔米对褚衡说：\"从今天起，我不再给你做助理。\" - 言语事件\nThe content of this statement implies she is declaring her resignation/termination of the assistant role. This is also a 计划 (she plans/determines not to be his assistant from today). But it's clearly a declared decision, so I should also record it as her decision/plan.\n\nLet me record:\n- 乔米对褚衡说\"从今天起，我不再给你做助理\" - 已发生 (speech)\n- 乔米决定从今天起不再做褚衡的助理 - 计划 (but this is somewhat redundant with the speech)\n\nActually, the speech IS the decision. The rules say \"已经说出口的询问、请求、命令、劝说、建议和评价，本身都按已经发生的言语事件记录\". This is a declaration, which is similar. I'll just record it as a speech event and also note the commitment/decision.\n\nHmm, let me think. \"从今天起，我不再给你做助理\" is a declarative statement about her own future action/state. It's both a speech event AND a decision. I think it's cleanest to record it as the speech event with the content, and the status is 已发生 (because the speech happened). The decision aspect can be noted through the content of the fact.\n\nFact 3: 褚衡没有把工牌还回去\nFact 4: 褚衡把卡片翻过去\nFact 5: 褚衡伸手把两人中间那条一直共用的抽屉锁上\nFact 6: 乔米和褚衡之间有一条一直共用的抽屉\nFact 7: 乔米站在原处看了褚衡两秒\nFact 8: 乔米把桌上那支共用的红笔推进抽屉缝\nFact 9: 乔米转身走了\nFact 10: 乔米和褚衡共有一支红笔\nFact 11: 此前乔米是褚衡的助理 (implied from her statement) - 推测? No, it's stated by 乔米 as fact. I think this is established.\n\nLet me think about the implied \"was his assistant before\" fact. The text says \"我不再给你做助理\" - \"I no longer will be your assistant.\" This directly implies she WAS his assistant. The speaker is 乔米. I'll record it with speaker.\n\nActually, on reflection, the fact that she was his assistant is clearly established by the statement. It's not a 推测 - she is stating it as fact. But the source is 乔米 (she said it), so it needs a speaker. Or actually, it's established by the statement that she was his assistant. Since the text uses \"我不再\" which presupposes she was, this is established as